1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,720
The fake diaries had the wrong letters on the cover.

2
00:00:03,160 --> 00:00:05,920
And a huge magazine still paid a fortune for them.

3
00:00:06,460 --> 00:00:09,080
Here's the story. West Germany, the early nineteen eighties.

4
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:13,660
A man named Konrad Kujau sells old war souvenirs.

5
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:18,220
Then he starts hand-writing notebooks, and says they're Hitler's secret diaries.

6
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:22,820
But a star reporter at Stern, a big German magazine, fell for it hard.

7
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:24,840
Tap the heart if you saw that coming.

8
00:00:25,420 --> 00:00:29,880
His name was Gerd Heidemann, and he got his bosses to pay about nine million marks.

9
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:34,300
Marks were German money back then. Think a fortune, for some notebooks.

10
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:38,120
And Heidemann? He secretly kept a big chunk of that cash.

11
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:42,000
In April nineteen eighty-three, the magazine tells the whole world.

12
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:45,020
So what was wrong with the covers? The initials.

13
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:49,520
They were plastic letters from a shop. And they actually said F H.

14
00:00:50,060 --> 00:00:54,220
But Hitler's first name starts with an A, so he got it wrong, right on the front.

15
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:56,920
Send this to the friend who never proofreads.

16
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:00,740
Then Germany's national archives tested the paper and the ink.

17
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:05,940
Both were modern. Less than two weeks after the announcement, they called it a crude forgery.

18
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:08,980
In plain words? A cheap, obvious fake.

19
00:01:09,540 --> 00:01:12,220
Follow if you love a scam that dies on one typo.

20
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:15,900
In nineteen eighty-five, a Hamburg court convicted both men.

21
00:01:16,660 --> 00:01:19,460
Kujau and Heidemann each got about four and a half years in prison.

22
00:01:20,140 --> 00:01:23,020
Nine million marks, sunk by two little letters.

23
00:01:23,020 --> 00:01:25,480
Would you have spotted it? Yes or no.

